WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:10.860
Cool, so we've got our little character here
in the forest, hopping along and the grid

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:16.379
outdoors, so happy to
be outside, wild and free.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.820
Now, what we're going to do is we're going
to add some obstacles to make this a little

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:28.220
bit more game-like, so we're going to go
into our assets folder, go to our obstacles,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.721
go, oh, kind of like
this barrier, kind of

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:37.940
looks like a fence, so
we'll go and drop this

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:43.980
into our hierarchy, and we're just going to
position this a little farther back, let's

00:00:44.029 --> 00:00:47.700
call it, let's put it like the edge of the
screen, like right there, cool, perfect.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.648
So now that we have
our barrier, you can see

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.620
that it has nothing for
components, so we're

00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:56.364
going to have to add
some things like a box

00:00:56.376 --> 00:00:59.260
collider, so that the
player can collide with

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:08.197
it, cool, and we'll
just resize this box

00:01:08.209 --> 00:01:11.660
collider really quick,
so we've set up our box

00:01:11.661 --> 00:01:14.278
collider so that it
looks really nice, cool,

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.860
that's perfect, now
we're actually going to

00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:25.298
add a rigid body, so
now this is an actual

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.280
physical object in the
scene that the player

00:01:27.281 --> 00:01:31.260
can actually run into and collide with, and
it'll use physics, so it might topple over

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:34.273
if you run into it, if
you notice, we actually

00:01:34.285 --> 00:01:36.820
didn't check the is
trigger box on the box

00:01:36.919 --> 00:01:39.324
collider, that's because
this isn't actually a

00:01:39.336 --> 00:01:41.700
collider that will have
us destroy the object

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:46.260
or anything, it's just so that we know when
we run into it, and then we're just going

00:01:46.261 --> 00:01:53.540
to rename this barrier, this fence really
quick, and we're going to call it obstacle,

00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:55.913
now what we're going
to do is in our assets

00:01:55.925 --> 00:01:58.420
folder, we're going to
make a prefab, because

00:01:58.421 --> 00:02:02.196
we're going to use this
again, so we're going

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:08.867
to make a prefab's folder, and then we'll
take our obstacle, and we'll left click,

00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:12.420
drag it down into
prefabs, so now we'll make

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.474
an original prefab, and
here you can see that

00:02:19.486 --> 00:02:26.368
we have this fence saved, and now that we
have this prefab saved, we're actually going

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.460
to make it move in the
scene, so we're going

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:37.860
to make a script, and we'll call it move
left, very simple name, because it'll just

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.431
make things move left,
so now we'll take the

00:02:43.443 --> 00:02:46.780
move left script,
apply it to our obstacle,

00:02:46.781 --> 00:02:49.863
and then just make
sure that we override our

00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:52.900
obstacle to apply it
to all of our prefabs,

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.468
and then in our move
left script, we're just

00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:01.407
going to open it up really quick, now inside
of our move left script, we're going to

00:03:01.419 --> 00:03:05.380
create a variable for
speed, so this will just

00:03:05.381 --> 00:03:08.632
be private, and it'll
be a float, because we

00:03:08.644 --> 00:03:11.760
can always just edit
it inside of our code

00:03:13.255 --> 00:03:20.980
later, we'll call it speed, and we'll set
it to 30 for now, and then we're actually

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:22.928
going to move this
using our transform.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.540
translate once again instead
of trying to use physics

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.403
to move a fence, so
we'll just transform

00:03:31.415 --> 00:03:35.860
translate, like we always
do, and then we're going

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:50.967
to move it to the left, since the fence
is to the right of the player, so vector 3.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:54.999
left, we want this to move
over time instead of moving

00:03:55.011 --> 00:03:58.018
every single frame,
so we'll use time.

00:04:08.598 --> 00:04:10.656
delta time, and then we'll
move it at the speed that

00:04:10.668 --> 00:04:15.835
we set, and then if we save, so now in unity
when we press play, our fence flies at a

00:04:15.847 --> 00:04:19.660
really fast speed at
the player, and I think

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:22.646
we're just flying off
into the distance, there

00:04:22.658 --> 00:04:25.260
it goes, so we can
always change the speed

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.333
of that to something
less later, what we can

00:04:29.345 --> 00:04:33.300
do for now is because
we're actually making

00:04:33.301 --> 00:04:36.962
look like the player is
running, we're actually

00:04:36.974 --> 00:04:43.094
just going to move everything around the
player to make it look like they're running,

00:04:43.106 --> 00:04:46.180
so if we actually take
this move left script,

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.980
then we apply it to our background, this
now creates the illusion when we press play,

00:04:56.155 --> 00:04:58.753
that our player is
running through the scene,

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.260
even though in fact
the player's not moving

00:05:01.261 --> 00:05:05.340
at all, you're going to make the player look
like they're moving, so what you're going

00:05:05.341 --> 00:05:09.071
to do is grab an obstacle
from the obstacles

00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:12.740
folder, create it, make
sure that you add a

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:18.740
box collider, a rigid body, if you want you
can even add the move left script now, then

00:05:18.741 --> 00:05:21.425
add it to your scripts
folder, and then you can

00:05:21.437 --> 00:05:24.020
create your prefabs
folder, drag the obstacle

00:05:24.021 --> 00:05:30.980
down into prefabs, and then your move left
script, you're going to give it a speed, so

00:05:30.981 --> 00:05:38.060
just set it for 30 for now, in your update
method you're just going to move it through

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.373
translating the transform,
so we're going to

00:05:41.385 --> 00:05:44.660
move it to the left,
over time add a certain

00:05:44.835 --> 00:05:47.703
speed, and then a
nice little effect that you

00:05:47.715 --> 00:05:50.660
can do is on your
background, you can actually

00:05:50.661 --> 00:05:52.888
add the move left
script, so then that way

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.300
when you press play,
it looks like the player

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.131
is moving to the
right, when in fact

00:05:57.143 --> 00:06:11.220
everything else is moving
to the left, now it's your turn.